[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2556056570","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100619#issuecomment-2556056570","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100619","id":2556056570,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YWlP6","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T01:13:11Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T01:14:53Z","body":"Hrm. I'm kinda stumped as to what's leaking. I _think_ it's foolproof, in any case foolproof if the `CowData` itself is not accessed from other threads (though access of `refcount` should be safe cross-thread). And besides, the previous implementation was also not safe from forking a 1-ref'd CowData from another thread, I think (through `realloc`). Either I'm missing some odd edge case or race condition, or something fishy is going on.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2556056570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557765627","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100619#issuecomment-2557765627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100619","id":2557765627,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YdGf7","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T21:54:56Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T21:54:56Z","body":"Oh my god... This leak is costing me and arm and a leg to debug. Here is a failing log for reference: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/12435300159/job/34720869143\r\n\r\nI have finally tracked it down to the GDScript tests _only_. Normal operation does not appear to cause leaks. At this point, I am reasonably sure it's not my implementation that's causing it, but some kind of circular reference. Though it's hard to be completely certain.\r\nIf it is a circular reference, the current implementation of `CowData` appears to 'avoid' it somehow, but it's really hard to track down and I have, so far, not been able to re-create the bug / fix in my refactor by attempting to recreate CowData behavior in that class.\r\n\r\nRunning the unit tests locally without `out_of_order_external.gd` avoids the leak. Online, I had to disable all GDScript unit tests, because more than just one were causing the leak. But disabling them _does_ avoid any leaks from appearing: https://github.com/Ivorforce/godot/actions/runs/12438440843\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557765627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557813233","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100619#issuecomment-2557813233","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100619","id":2557813233,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YdSHx","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-20T22:23:16Z","updated_at":"2024-12-20T22:23:16Z","body":"![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a41e9074-7697-4b84-89a5-ab1a660a66dc)\r\n\r\nI'll look at this PR over the weekend. I have a suspicion but it'll take some single stepping, and Friday night is not the time for single stepping through CowData.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557813233/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":5,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557936334","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100619#issuecomment-2557936334","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100619","id":2557936334,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YdwLO","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T01:22:36Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T01:22:36Z","body":"I have an update. Turns out one of the 'preconditions' I was imagining to be true was false all along - `refcount` can be 0. Who knew.\r\n\r\nThis is true on master as well, as this fails unit tests: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/master...Ivorforce:godot:cowdata-refcount-0\r\n\r\nAfter meticulously re-creating my PR step by step, I'm pretty sure that's what's causing the issues. I don't know how it's possible that `refcount` is 0 at any time. At least in this PR, it's initialized with 1 and decremented and incremented in very controlled ways, and I recently checked [nobody else is interfering](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100650). This is a really strange one...","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2557936334/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558097297","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100619#issuecomment-2558097297","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100619","id":2558097297,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YeXeR","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-21T12:05:20Z","updated_at":"2024-12-21T12:24:08Z","body":"I think I finally fixed it.\r\n\r\nSo, `GDScript` _does_ have cyclic references, and it calls a `Vector` destructor, and then halfway through the destruction, the array is referenced again through some pointer. We should probably figure out that cyclic reference, because it _really_ smells. But it's out of scope for me to address it (for posterity, involved functions are logged [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/12435300159/job/34720869143) - one is `constants` in `GDScriptFunction`).\r\n\r\nInstead, I managed to handle it more graciously through #100694. With the change, `CowData` invalidates itself _before_ destructing the array, and graciously handles being referenced, reallocated, or re-deallocated halfway through its own destruction. We'll see if the remote leak sanitizers agree, but this fixed the leak on my end.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2558097297/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571263728","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100619#issuecomment-2571263728","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100619","id":2571263728,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZQl7w","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"